{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-16T03:33:29.042Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"aafa2be13b294c2b9a62368a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-0m64xk","claim:pm-wb6ktl","claim:pm-womkyw","lineage:pm-0m64xk","lineage:pm-dj98","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-0m64xk+pm-wb6ktl+pm-womkyw","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-0m64xk","claim:pm-wb6ktl","claim:pm-womkyw","lineage:pm-0m64xk","lineage:pm-dj98","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-16T03:33:29.042Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-16T03:33:29.041Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Implementation note (2026-11-16): the coordinator now opens a journal-proven rollback scope (ItemMutationPrecondition.compensation: transaction_id, step_id, operations, overrides) in compensateCreatedItem and compensateByRestore, only after the existing history-ownership proof and inside the locked hash precondition. runActiveBeforeMutationHooks and enforceWorkflowMutation look the scope up by tracker root + either item identity + operation. Guards receive a frozen compensation {transaction_id, step_id}; a denial, thrown error or timeout becomes a MutationGuardOverride instead of a refusal. Workflow-policy refusals are recorded the same way, because a policy refusing close/delete/restore wedged the rollback identically (verified on main: 'Workflow policy refused close: release-close (authors)' inside the AggregateError). The close/delete/restore history entry records context.transaction_compensation.overridden only when something was overridden, so ordinary compensation bytes are unchanged. Dry runs never exempt. Negative controls: a write to another item in the scope, another operation, and an ordinary close reusing the compensation message are all judged normally. runRegisteredMutationGuardForTest/harness.runMutationGuard now return the overrides (empty outside a rollback). Reproduced on unmodified main in a detached worktree: 3 rollback specs failed with 'Workspace transaction failed and compensation failed'; all pass on the branch."}]}],"before_hash":"d6e0f01bd257b6635879c21ae6a76b1574598c2474039743b94ffb2b9439e51c","after_hash":"f8ec19c30c4add5442fcdbad384f9b4fdf97f58183acfffc34cf1fbedba22148","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"d73dd998bcb1871a5a139f3c52f1d8116dde1328dae15b91b15eafbf3f6072a4"}
