{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-16T05:51:06.684Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"aafa2be13b294c2b9a62368a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-16T05:51:06.684Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review fix (PR 1740, Codex gpt-6.1-sol round 1, P1): runActiveBeforeMutationHooks spread the caller's input into the guard context, so a JS caller could hand it its own compensation block and have denials recorded instead of enforced (types omitted the field, runtime did not). The guard context is now built from an explicit allowlist (pm_root, operation, before, after, changed_fields, sdk) plus the host-resolved actor, dry_run and scope-derived compensation; the spec proves a forged compensation is never seen by the guard and the denial still refuses. Round 1 P2: the test helper's widened return type broke Promise<void> utilities (TS2322); runRegisteredMutationGuardForTest and harness.runMutationGuard now use overloads (rollback context -> MutationGuardOverride[], ordinary -> Promise<void>), pinned by tests/types/mutation-guard-rollback.test-d.ts."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-16T05:51:06.684Z"}],"before_hash":"12587c33543ae11ca28c51d29828c3c0479d6c1f78411b130f4e32134fecef35","after_hash":"017dc64f50f1e6c92a7446386ba1559db01d862da39f284846b8c724f95c885f","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"re