{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-16T06:16:06.247Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"aafa2be13b294c2b9a62368a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-16T06:16:06.246Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review fix (PR 1740, Codex gpt-6.1-sol round 2, two P1s; CodeRabbit full review, one minor). P1: the public SDK re-exports the compensation helpers through the item-transaction test-only export, and the legacy restore receipt is identified by a free-form history message alone, so a direct helper call could claim the exemption without any coordinator journal. The exemption now also requires that the workspace-transaction coordinator itself is compensating that exact transaction step (a private AsyncLocalStorage scope in src/core/store/transaction-coordinator-scope.ts, opened only around step.compensate in compensateAppliedSteps), and that the proof is history-bound: a create whose whole history belongs to the transaction, or a restore receipt bound to the captured history prefix. A legacy message-only receipt keeps normal enforcement. P1: the lookup trusted the proposed after.metadata.id, so a write to B proposing id A borrowed A's scope. Now every identity the write carries must equal the scoped id, and assertItemMutationPreconditions marks the scope validated only when the ownership validator held against the locked item whose storage id is the scoped id. CodeRabbit minor: runRegisteredMutationGuardForTest now drops compensation on dry runs, matching the host. Both new specs (direct helper call outside the coordinator; proposed-id and unvalidated scope) fail on the round-1 head c250e909d and pass now.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-16T06:16:06.247Z"}],"before_hash":"1311c4b3536149367db792793bc42c2e371675aa089fc9e5bfcd65f9ecea69eb","after_hash":"71dfcdfe9e5b7a3e7cf7da8f5c72a26465cb8db26c86f20d0bd4b12541a5cc93","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"315d355d0c5e7d95ab393a48c1375b52a09c24a5430bd33ef36612106d26f7dc"}
