Z"}],"before_hash":"71dfcdfe9e5b7a3e7cf7da8f5c72a26465cb8db26c86f20d0bd4b12541a5cc93","after_hash":"757cd61be5fc4434dc1b04a13409c5fcb17709784395853bf7cffdb7ffb7f75b","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"maintenance","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"8a7484edff5b9d300c4220061fad320780ce486c034e1e73f3d28a8834a4d3f8"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-16T06:35:30.211Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"aafa2be13b294c2b9a62368a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-16T06:35:30.211Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review fix (PR 1740, Codex round 3 P1): matching the coordinator's ambient transaction and step strings still let a caller pass its own step to commitWorkspaceTransaction whose compensation called the exported compensateByRestore helper with a computed history-prefix receipt, after a forged step-marker update the caller was allowed to make. The coordinator scope now carries the step object it compensates, and the exemption requires that object to be registered in a private WeakMap by buildStepForMutation, the only builder the commit, preview and recovery paths use, for exactly this transaction, step id, item id and operation. Raw builders exported for tests stay unregistered. New spec: the caller-supplied step's restore is refused, so the batch reports compensation failed and the forged title remains; it fails on the round-2 commit 3e8d2bde0. Round 3 P2: the lease specs now age the slow writer's lock record instead of sleeping out a TTL, and park the fast writer in its own guard, so neither guard waits beyond a lock handoff (the spec runs in 1.5 s instead of 3.7 s and has no wall-clock race with the 5 s guard timeout).\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-16T06:35:30.211Z"}],"before_hash":"757cd61be5fc4434dc1b04a13409c5fcb17709784395853bf7cffdb7ffb7f75b","after_hash":"f0b7def6afa85906618ebfb9e0eff1966088166a678062cb1dcf58c348b4adbe","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"04b7983b07f988cee5e9a7b25da4ebd3faa8fb2d4141c8dcf8a2b7a6db376d2d"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-16T08:12:03.716Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"aafa2be13b294c2b9a62368a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-16T08:12:03.716Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review fix (PR 1740, CodeRabbit full review of ca00814a7, Major): decision validation ran outside the guard's error normalization, so a decision whose accessor throws a non-error value (for example a getter throwing null) escaped raw, and during a rollback the override recorder read code on null and crashed the rollback. Validation now runs inside the normalization block, so any such failure is the typed extension_mutation_guard_failed: refused on an ordinary write, recorded as an override during a rollback. Spec added."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-16T08:12:03.716Z"}],"before_hash":"f0b7def6afa85906618ebfb9e0eff1966088166a678062cb1dcf58c348b4adbe","after_hash":"8a56f06e0921d0c5919a070e80955a4d6b447464d142a4b8d12525db3d9ab043","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"abc1304e5ea7e64bee18326aa18b06081e1180b360315dd2a097fa3d88d942ef"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-16T11:17:39.042Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"aafa2be13b294c2b9a62368a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/5","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-16T11:17:39.041Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review fix (PR 1740, CodeRabbit full review of 625d8c0d5, Minor): the ownership proof read the item's history before the item lock, and the locked validator compared only the document hash with that stale snapshot's head after_hash. A foreign write that lands after the proof and is later reverted to the same document hash (an ABA sequence) passed the check, so the rollback exemption was granted from history that predates the foreign writes. compensateCreatedItem and compensateByRestore now read the history through readOwnershipHistory, which binds the proof to the exact bytes it read (one readHistorySnapshot call), and the locked validator re-reads the stream and refuses with transaction_partial_mutation when the bytes changed. The new spec makes a test extension's onRead hook append a foreign line right after the created item's rollback proof read: the rollback now refuses (compensation failed, the item stays open). Replacing the byte check with a constant true fails that spec.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-16T11:17:39.042Z"}],"before_hash":"8a56f06e0921d0c5919a070e80955a4d6b447464d142a4b8d12525db3d9ab043","after_hash":"2e9070e55b093e2dd3b0f29c245786b7db6d727c21afae7a0c56b721b655be79","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"bc6616fe0a9445e73b486a3f59b0e0a6e4ad6c01002a11b0d52bb5239fa891d7"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-16T12:21:55.519Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"aafa2be13b294c2b9a62368a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/6","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-16T12:21:55.519Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review fix (PR 1740, CodeRabbit full review of 7e8fdb3de, three Minor findings). First, the locked history recheck now compares the raw history bytes captured by the proof read (Buffer.equals against raw_bytes), never decoded UTF-8 text. Second, a stream that is unreadable or vanished after the proof read, or that was absent at proof time, now raises the typed transaction_partial_mutation refusal with the filesystem error kept as its cause, instead of leaking ENOENT; a spec deletes the history right after the proof read and asserts the typed refusal with cause ENOENT. Mutants without the byte check, and that rethrow the raw error, both fail the spec. Third, MutationGuardTestContext no longer carries compensation, so it is back to its pre-PR shape, and only RunRegisteredMutationGuardRollbackForTestOptions has it. The ordinary overload therefore rejects a compensation-bearing context while existing Promise<void> wrappers still compile, as tests/types/mutation-guard-rollback.test-d.ts pins.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-16T12:21:55.519Z"}],"before_hash":"2e9070e55b093e2dd3b0f29c245786b7db6d727c21afae7a0c56b721b655be79","after_hash":"6e909371a034cd64d39897c4b3d0cc5fe8237154078a3bbe6725ad44782819f6","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"725a6837722c346b89b39f1792f90fc0d22d7d80a40c576431291257fd37edf6"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-16T14:30:55.008Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"aafa2be13b294c2b9a62368a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/7","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-16T14:30:55.007Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Hosted Gates (coverage) on 10ce5310c found two uncovered lines, the document-hash refusals after the new byte check (item-transaction.ts 593 and 702). Every foreign write through pm also appends history, so the byte check refuses first, and the hash refusal became reachable only through an unlocked item-file edit that leaves history untouched. The two checks are now one locked ownership assertion (assertOwnedUnderLock): byte-identical history AND the locked document equal to the newest entry's after_hash. A new spec edits the item file right after the proof read without touching history, and the rollback refuses with transaction_partial_mutation. A mutant without the hash half fails it."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-16T14:30:55.008Z"}],"before_hash":"6e909371a034cd64d39897c4b3d0cc5fe8237154078a3bbe6725ad44782819f6","after_hash":"92e91865194f245e8cfb53d3c0ae95a68d0a8f1151e85266e372cd84d3a501a1","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"1cb7b218936e5b7b04ebb5f1a8ec2300c2e7d83bcd0cea4dce75b291d3efe6c1"}
